<!--
  The AI Outreach integration user's permission set (outreach spec 2026-10-04,
  section 5). Assign it to the Salesforce Integration user that
  services/outreach-api connects as - never to reps.

  What it grants, and why each part is needed:
  - read + edit on the three AI Call Consent fields on Lead and Opportunity:
    the outbox (services/outreach-api/src/crm/outbox.ts) writes captured consent;
  - read + edit on DoNotCall / HasOptedOutOfEmail on Lead and Contact: a
    confirmed do-not-contact sets them (Opportunity has no such fields, so the
    primary contact role's Contact is updated instead);
  - read on the standard phone, email and description fields the campaign
    engine reads, and on Skip_on_Dialer__c;
  - read + edit + View All on Lead, Opportunity, Contact and Account; no
    delete and no Modify All anywhere. AI Outreach
    creates Events, Tasks and Chatter posts, and converts a Lead that booked an appointment; never deletes;
  - Edit Tasks, and edit on Activity.CTI_Origin__c, for the AI Outreach Task
    marker on the Events and Tasks it creates;
  - read + edit on AI_Last_Call_Changes__c on Lead and Opportunity: the plan 1D
    write-back records there what it changed after each AI call;
  - Edit Events: the plan 1D write-back puts a booked appointment on the
    appointment owner's calendar;
  - Convert Leads, plus create on Account, Contact and Opportunity: the plan 1D
    write-back converts a Lead that booked an appointment (decision 2), through
    the SOAP API's convertLead (a conversion creates a Person Account, a
    Contact and an Opportunity). A System Administrator already has these; a
    dedicated connected user needs them from here. Lead itself gets no create.

  The tenant's qualification fields get edit through the in-org
  AI_Outreach_Fields permission set, not here. Record type access (Person
  Account, Homeowner Opportunity) and edit on Opportunity.LeadManager__c are
  tenant-specific too and are granted in-org (docs/runbooks/outreach-sf-campaigns.md),
  so this file still deploys to any org.

  Tenant-specific custom fields (notes, extra phone fields, web form source,
  lead manager) are NOT here: they exist only in that tenant's org, and a
  reference to a missing field fails the whole deploy. The runbook
  (docs/runbooks/outreach-sf-campaigns.md, Salesforce setup) grants them
  in-org instead.

  The API name is load-bearing: the runbook and salesforce-metadata.test.ts
  refer to it by AI_Outreach.
-->
